GRA-20 -- kgraphMapBd part-count check compared a value with its own copy; OOM path leaked
==========================================================================================
kgraph_map_bd.c copied bndgrafdat.m.domnnbr into orggrafptr->m.domnnbr and only
then tested `bndgrafdat.m.domnnbr != orggrafptr->m.domnnbr' -- always false, so a
band strategy that changes the number of parts was never rejected and the original
graph was left with an inconsistent (domnnbr, comploaddlt, frontab). The fix
compares against the `domnnbr' local captured at entry and does not overwrite
orggrafptr->m.domnnbr before the test.

Reproducer gra20.c: 2-part mapping of a 24x24 grid onto cmplt(8); a band strategy
`r{sep=h{pass=10}}' that re-maps from scratch creates 8 parts.
  cc.sh <build> GRA-20/gra20 GRA-20/gra20.c ; LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<build>/lib ./GRA-20/gra20
  pristine 7.0.17 : ret=0 changed=228 domnnbr=8   (silently accepted; part count corrupted 2 -> 8)
  patched         : ERROR "change in band graph number of parts not supported"; ret=1 domnnbr=2

Leak: the `orgflagtab' allocation-failure path returned without freeing bndvnumtax
or exiting bndgrafdat, unlike the two earlier failure paths in the same routine
(out of memory (1), cannot partition band graph), which free both. The fix makes it
match them. Verified by source inspection against those sibling paths; a runtime
proof needs allocation-failure injection on that specific call.
